{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-6034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}z}{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-6034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}z}{z} & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{6}^{a}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{z} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡z]}_{6}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡a-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6) \\\\  & =\\infty -\\operatorname{ln}⁡6 \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-6034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5eb3d2a0b8613cc7fa6de9ab06f80a39d1ce753a71b160010e72695f307e18c6"} {"question" "q-6034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-6034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)"] ["math" "{e}^{6}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-6034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The integral diverges"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-152779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{(z+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-152779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=z+2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $z\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=z+2$ is as follows:\n\n| $z$ | $-1$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{(z+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}z={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{(z+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{-3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-152779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5eb3d2a0b8613cc7fa6de9ab06f80a39d1ce753a71b160010e72695f307e18c6"} {"question" "q-152779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-152779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-152779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{(3y+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=3y+2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $y\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=3y+2$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{(3y+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{3{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{(3y+2)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{3{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{3}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{5}{3}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{5}{9}{u}^{-3}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-3}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{72}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5eb3d2a0b8613cc7fa6de9ab06f80a39d1ce753a71b160010e72695f307e18c6"} {"question" "q-350530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{72}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{10}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{10}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{x}^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{-5}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{a}^{5}}] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5eb3d2a0b8613cc7fa6de9ab06f80a39d1ce753a71b160010e72695f307e18c6"} {"question" "q-350537" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350537" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{6}{(2x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=2x+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2x+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{6}{(2x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u & =3{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{-3}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-(-1-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5eb3d2a0b8613cc7fa6de9ab06f80a39d1ce753a71b160010e72695f307e18c6"} {"question" "q-350540" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"} {"question" "q-350540" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062733/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b467a913288da06f6a4c27ba95b65f8b27d090f585a1d73124316d804ff2a66"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2023 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
